%% Top-down read flow for a Reactor perf trace. The user runs the app
%% under a profiler, picks the keywords they want, opens the resulting
%% file in a viewer, and reads the Reactor span hierarchy. Reactor-only
%% workflows use dotnet-trace + Speedscope/Visual Studio; correlated
%% Reactor + WinUI captures need ETW (PerfView / xperf / WPA) because
%% Microsoft-Windows-XAML is a native ETW provider that does not flow
%% through EventPipe. Default Mermaid palette renders legibly on both
%% light and dark GitHub themes.
flowchart TB
    App["Reactor app (Release build)"]
    Choice{"Which timeline do you need?"}

    subgraph EP["EventPipe path (Reactor only)"]
        direction TB
        Trace["dotnet-trace collect<br/>--providers Microsoft-UI-Reactor:0x3:4"]
        Nettrace[".nettrace file"]
        Speedscope["speedscope.app / VS Profiler"]
    end

    subgraph ETW["ETW path (Reactor + WinUI)"]
        direction TB
        PerfView["PerfView /<br/>xperf -on Microsoft-UI-Reactor + Microsoft-Windows-XAML"]
        Etl[".etl file"]
        WPA["PerfView Events view /<br/>WPA timeline"]
    end

    Spans["Reactor span hierarchy<br/>ReconcileStart/Stop · ChildReconcileStart/Stop ·<br/>ComponentRenderStart/Stop · EffectsFlushStart/Stop ·<br/>StateChange · EventTrampolineDispatch"]

    App --> Choice
    Choice -->|"Reactor-only,<br/>any OS"| Trace
    Choice -->|"frame stutter<br/>could be WinUI"| PerfView

    Trace --> Nettrace --> Speedscope --> Spans
    PerfView --> Etl --> WPA --> Spans

    Spans -.->|"sort by elapsed µs,<br/>find the outlier band"| Outlier["Slow reconcile pass /<br/>excessive child diff /<br/>unstable UseMemo deps"]
